/security-review — loop U5, round 1 — range 4ea824e..3967adf — 2026-09-19

NO FINDINGS on 4ea824e..HEAD. Nothing added by this branch meets the >80%-exploitable bar.

Terminal escape injection: every new attacker-derived string reaches a terminal only through sanitize. Bar: `project()` in src/modules/render/segments.rs:146-149 builds "{glyph} {name}" and returns it to `segment()`, which filters at segments.rs:55 (`super::sanitize(&text)`) before styling; nothing bypasses that path. `--doctor`: the new `project:` row (src/_runtime/app.rs:515-521) wraps the assembled `kind name (root)` in `field()` (app.rs:365-366, `crate::render::sanitize`) and the whole report is swept again by `sanitize_report` at app.rs:554. Narration: `narrate` (app.rs:136-140) goes through `crate::_shared::diag`, which sanitizes at src/_shared/mod.rs:48 before eprintln. `config.symbol()` is inside the same formatted string and so is filtered too.

Path traversal / data exposure: the resolver reads exactly four files — `<root>/.git` (pointer), `<gitdir>/HEAD`, `<gitdir>/commondir`, `<common>/config` (src/modules/git.rs:159, 168, 222, 226, 249). `gitdir:` and `commondir` contents are attacker-controlled and are joined without confinement (`normalise` is lexical, drops `..` above `/`), so the binary can be pointed at any directory. But what is disclosed from those reads is bounded: HEAD -> branch name/7 chars (pre-existing, `probe` predates this branch); commondir -> only used to build a path, and only the last two components (`parent_base`) or the path itself (`--doctor`, attacker already knows it) are shown; config -> only the `url` value under `[remote "origin"]`, and only its path part after host classification (authority incl. any embedded credential is discarded in `classify`, git.rs:293-296). Worst case: a tarball-distributed `.git` pointer file (git itself refuses to track a `.git` entry, so a plain clone cannot carry one) aimed at `/Users/victim/other-repo/.git` reveals that repo's origin org/repo path in the bar. Low impact, requires knowing the local path, below threshold — noted for completeness.

Command injection / subprocess: no new subprocess. `ahead_count`/`dirty_counts` (git.rs:387-416) still run `git` with fixed argv and cwd=root; the only attacker influence is the cwd, which is unchanged from before this branch. (Pre-existing, out of scope: running `git` inside a hostile clone lets its `.git/config` drive git behaviour, e.g. core.fsmonitor — not introduced here.)

Unbounded pointer following: `gitdir:` is dereferenced once, `commondir` once, `.git/modules` is a pure component scan of the already-resolved path (git.rs:235-240). No loop, no recursion.
